  "knowledge": {
    "insights": [
      "Index 2 is the single structural lever: a subgroup of index 2 is normal with an order-2 quotient, so g² ∈ H for every g — no element enumeration needed.",
      "Every 3-cycle is a square: order 3 gives σ = σ⁴ = (σ²)², so the 'all squares inside' property of an index-2 subgroup drags every 3-cycle into H.",
      "Generation closes the argument: since the 3-cycles generate A₄ (`closure_three_cycles_eq_alternating`), an order-6 subgroup containing them all would be the whole group, contradicting |H| = 6.",
      "|A₄| = 12 is obtained from `card_alternatingGroup` (n!/2) closed by kernel `decide`, which adds no axioms — the key difference from the parent's `native_decide`/`Lean.ofReduceBool` route.",
      "Cardinality transport across the injective inclusion A₄ ↪ Perm(Fin 4) via `equivMapOfInjective` lets the whole argument live one level up among permutations while the contradiction is read off downstairs."
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "a4_card: Fintype.card (alternatingGroup (Fin 4)) = 12 via card_alternatingGroup + kernel decide (LagrangeTheoremOQ03OQ02.lean:49)",
      "sq_mem_of_index_two: index-2 normal subgroup contains every square (LagrangeTheoremOQ03OQ02.lean:55)",
      "index_two_of_card_six: an order-6 subgroup of A₄ has index 2 (LagrangeTheoremOQ03OQ02.lean:66)",
      "a4_no_subgroup_order_six: the main 0-axiom non-existence theorem (LagrangeTheoremOQ03OQ02.lean:76)",
      "lagrange_converse_fails: bundles 6 | |A₄| with the non-existence (LagrangeTheoremOQ03OQ02.lean:125)"
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [
      "Mathlib has the A₄ counterexample only implicitly; there is no off-the-shelf lemma 'A₄ has no subgroup of order 6', so the generation-based argument is assembled here from card_alternatingGroup, closure_three_cycles_eq_alternating, and normal_of_index_eq_two."
    ],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Generalize the 'index 2 ⟹ all squares ⟹ generators inside' template to other forbidden subgroup orders in larger alternating groups.",
      "Assemble the full subgroup-order spectrum of A₄ (only 1, 2, 3, 4, 12 are realized) structurally from the same generation and Sylow ingredients."
    ],
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: 0-axiom, 0-sorry structural proof that A₄ has no subgroup of order 6, removing the parent entry's native_decide / Lean.ofReduceBool dependency. #print axioms reports only propext / Classical.choice / Quot.sound."
  },
